.TH SSH\-SELECTOR 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2edaq-cluster-tools 1.0.1" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
ssh\-selector \- terminal UI for picking and connecting to SSH hosts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssh\-selector
.RB [ \-c
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-check\-concurrency
.IR N ]
.br
.B ssh\-selector
.BR \-\-version | \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ssh\-selector
is a Textual terminal UI over a YAML host list.
Hosts are shown in named groups, two per row, and can be filtered by
nickname or hostname.
Each host may have several login users, a non-default port and a ProxyJump
host.
The tool builds and runs
.BR ssh (1)
command lines; it holds no credentials and reads no
.I ~/.ssh/config
of its own, although
.B ssh
does.
.PP
The right-hand panel shows the highlighted host's details and the
.B ssh
command for its first user, the output of
.BR klist (1)
refreshed every 60 s with expiry colouring (green over 2 h, yellow under,
red expired), the local hostname, IP and IPv4 subnets, and the background
tunnels started since
.B ssh\-selector
was launched (they stay listed across connections).
.PP
At start-up every hostname is resolved with
.BR gethostbyname (3);
the dot next to a host shows whether the name resolved, not whether the host
answers.
If a host has a ProxyJump and its resolved address lies inside one of the
local IPv4 subnets, the jump is skipped.
.PP
Choosing a host (Enter) leaves the UI and runs
.B ssh
in the current terminal; when the session ends the UI comes back.
.BR ssh 's
standard error is passed through to the terminal as it is written, so its
warnings are seen during the session; the last 8 KiB are also kept.
If
.B ssh
exits with status 255 (its own failure: name resolution, connection,
authentication, jump host) that text is shown in the "SSH Connection Failed"
dialog when the UI comes back.
Any other status is the remote shell's and raises no dialog.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " \fIFILE\fR"
YAML host file.
Overrides
.B SSH_SELECTOR_CONFIG
and skips discovery.
.TP
.BI \-\-check\-concurrency " N"
Maximum number of
.B ssh
processes "Check Users" runs at once (a positive integer).
Overrides
.B SSH_SELECTOR_CHECK_CONCURRENCY
and the
.B check_concurrency
config key.
Default 8.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print
.B ssh\-selector
.I version
and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.SH CONFIG FILE DISCOVERY
The host file is chosen by the first of these that applies:
.IP 1. 4
.B \-c
.IR FILE .
.IP 2. 4
.BR SSH_SELECTOR_CONFIG ,
a file path; a leading
.I ~
is expanded.
.IP 3. 4
Discovery.
Directories are searched in tiers; the first tier holding any
.I *.yaml
file supplies all candidates and later tiers are not consulted:
.RS
.IP a. 3
.I ./
and
.I ./config/
(relative to the current directory, merged in that order);
.IP b. 3
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mu2edaq/cluster\-tools/ ,
by default
.IR ~/.config/mu2edaq/cluster\-tools/ ;
.IP c. 3
.IR <install\ dir>/config/ ,
where the install directory is
.B MU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_TOOLS_INSTALL_DIR
if set, else the parent of the running venv when it carries the
.BR install.sh (1)
marker file
.IR .mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools\-install .
.RE
.PP
Duplicates by real path are dropped.
One candidate is loaded directly; several are offered in a picker; none is an
error that lists the directories searched.
A file named by
.B \-c
or
.B SSH_SELECTOR_CONFIG
that does not exist is an error; there is no fallback to discovery.
.PP
.I *.yml
and
.I *.yaml.example
files are not candidates.
Any other
.I *.yaml
file in a searched directory is, so keep non-host YAML (for example
.B lan\-scan
profiles) out of them; such a file stops with "No hosts defined".
.SH CONFIGURATION
Top-level keys:
.TP
.B hosts
Required list.
Each entry needs
.BR hostname ;
optional
.B nickname
(default the hostname),
.BR group ,
.B port
(default 22),
.B users
or
.B user
(a list or a scalar; the first is the default login),
.B proxy_jump
and
.BR proxy_user .
.TP
.B grouplist
Display order of group names.
Groups used by hosts but not listed follow in order of first use; hosts with no
group appear under "Other".
.TP
.B groups
Per-group defaults:
.BR users ,
.BR proxy_jump ,
.BR proxy_user .
A host key that is present, even as
.BR null ,
overrides the group value.
.TP
.B cache_lifetime
Seconds a "Check Users" result stays fresh.
Default 600.
.TP
.B panel_width
Width of the right-hand panel in columns.
Default 50.
.TP
.B check_concurrency
Maximum simultaneous "Check Users" connections.
Default 8.
Overridden by
.B SSH_SELECTOR_CHECK_CONCURRENCY
and
.BR \-\-check\-concurrency .
.PP
The user
.B default
means the current login name
.RB ( $USER ).
The jump user is
.B proxy_user
when set, else the destination user, unless
.B proxy_jump
already contains
.BR user@ .
The resulting commands are
.PP
.RS
.nf
ssh [\-p PORT] [\-J JUMPUSER@JUMPHOST] \-l USER HOST
ssh \-N \-o ExitOnForwardFailure=yes \-L LOCAL:localhost:REMOTE [\-p PORT] [\-J ...] \-l USER HOST
.fi
.RE
.PP
.I settings.md
in the source tree is the full reference;
.I config/hosts.yaml.example
is an annotated example.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.TP
.B Enter
Connect in the current terminal.
A user picker appears when the host has more than one user.
.TP
.B n
Connect in a new terminal window: Terminal.app via
.BR osascript (1)
on macOS; on Linux and other Unix systems the first of
.BR gnome\-terminal ,
.BR xfce4\-terminal ,
.BR konsole ,
.B xterm
found on
.B PATH
(looked up in-process, not with
.BR which (1)),
given the
.B ssh
command as separate arguments
.RB ( "gnome\-terminal \-\-" ,
.BR "xfce4\-terminal \-x" ,
.BR "konsole \-e" ,
.BR "xterm \-e" );
on Windows a new console window running
.BR ssh .
The host list is then rebuilt, as after a foreground session.
.TP
.B t
Port-forward tunnel.
Prompts for a local and a remote port (1\-65535) and a background switch
(default on).
Before starting, the local port is checked: if a background tunnel of this
session already forwards it, or anything else is listening on 127.0.0.1 or ::1
at that port, the tunnel is not started and a dialog says why.
In the background the tunnel is a child
.B ssh \-N
process in its own session (so Ctrl-C in a later foreground session does not
reach it), listed in the Tunnels panel for the life of the
.B ssh\-selector
process, including after Enter, n or a foreground t rebuild the UI.
Its standard error goes to a temporary log file; if the tunnel exits (for
example a forward that cannot be bound, which
.B ExitOnForwardFailure=yes
turns into an exit), it is removed from the panel and a dialog shows its exit
status and the end of that log.
In the foreground the UI exits, the tunnel runs until Ctrl-C, and the UI
comes back.
.TP
.B c
"Check Users": runs
.B ssh \-o BatchMode=yes \-o ConnectTimeout=5 ... who
against
.I every
host in the file, as each host's first user and through its jump host,
and shows the number of lines
.B who
prints.
At most
.B check_concurrency
(default 8, below OpenSSH's default
.B MaxStartups
of 10) connections run at once; the rest wait.
Each probe has a 12 s limit, after which its
.B ssh
is killed and the host is shown as unreachable; a non-zero
.B ssh
exit is also shown as unreachable.
Results are reused for
.B cache_lifetime
seconds, and pressing
.B c
again while a check is running does not start a second probe of the same host.
.TP
.B /
Focus the filter field.
.TP
.B r
Run
.B kinit \-R
(renew the current ticket) and refresh the panel.
.TP
.B A
About screen.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
If background tunnels are running, a dialog lists them and asks:
.B s
(or
.BR y )
stops them and quits,
.B k
leaves them running and quits (their PIDs and log files are printed),
.B Escape
(or
.BR n )
returns to the host list.
.TP
.B Left\fR, \fBRight
Move between the two hosts of a row.
.TP
.B Escape
In the filter field, clear it and return to the list; elsewhere, quit.
In a dialog, cancel it.
.PP
In the Tunnels panel,
.B k
or
.B Delete
sends SIGTERM to the highlighted background tunnel.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ./*.yaml\fR, \fI./config/*.yaml
Discovered host files, first tier.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mu2edaq/cluster\-tools/*.yaml
Per-user host files, second tier
(under
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
when set).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/mu2edaq\-cluster\-tools/config/*.yaml
Topology files copied by
.BR install.sh (1)
(default install directory), third tier.
.TP
.I config/mu2e_daq.yaml
Mu2e DAQ topology (75 hosts in 13 groups).
.TP
.I config/nova_daq.yaml\fR, \fIconfig/mu2e_offline.yaml\fR, \fIconfig/fnal_gpvm.yaml
NOvA DAQ, Mu2e offline and Fermilab GPVM host lists.
.TP
.I config/hosts.yaml.example\fR, \fIconfig/example.yaml
Annotated examples.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SSH_SELECTOR_CONFIG
Host file to load when
.B \-c
is not given.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base of the per-user config directory (default
.IR ~/.config ).
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_CLUSTER_TOOLS_INSTALL_DIR
Install directory whose
.I config/
is the last discovery tier; also read by
.BR install.sh (1).
.TP
.B USER
Login name used for the
.B default
user (falls back to
.BR getpass.getuser ()).
.TP
.B SSH_SELECTOR_CHECK_CONCURRENCY
Maximum simultaneous "Check Users" connections; overrides the
.B check_concurrency
config key and is overridden by
.BR \-\-check\-concurrency .
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Directory for the background tunnels' standard-error logs
.RI ( ssh\-selector\-tunnel\-PORT\-*.log ),
deleted when the tunnel is stopped or reported.
.TP
.B KRB5CCNAME
Not read directly; honoured by
.BR klist ,
.B kinit
and
.BR ssh .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Quit from the host list or the config picker.
.TP
.B 1
No config file found, the
.B \-c
or
.B SSH_SELECTOR_CONFIG
file does not exist, the file fails to load, it defines no hosts, or the
check concurrency from the command line, environment or file is not a positive
integer.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command line.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
ssh\-selector \-c config/mu2e_daq.yaml
ssh\-selector \-c config/nova_daq.yaml \-\-check\-concurrency 4
SSH_SELECTOR_CHECK_CONCURRENCY=2 ssh\-selector
cd ~/clusters && ssh\-selector        # pick among ./*.yaml
SSH_SELECTOR_CONFIG=~/hosts.yaml ssh\-selector
mkdir \-p ~/.config/mu2edaq/cluster\-tools && cp hosts.yaml ~/.config/mu2edaq/cluster\-tools/
.fi
.RE
.SH BUGS
Background tunnels are stopped when
.B ssh\-selector
exits normally or receives SIGHUP or SIGTERM, unless the user chose to keep
them at quit; a SIGKILL leaves them running.
.SH KERBEROS SUPPORT
Ticket display and renewal need
.B klist
and
.B kinit
on
.BR PATH .
On Windows this works within WSL and from PowerShell when Kerberos is
configured; MIT Kerberos for Windows has compatibility issues with some
terminal emulators.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lan\-scan (1),
.BR ssh (1),
.BR klist (1),
.BR kinit (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andrew Norman, Mu2e DAQ Group, Fermi National Accelerator Laboratory.
